INT. LATE-NIGHT NOODLE BAR - NIGHT

Steam. Fluorescent. Six stools at a counter, two booths. A neon sign buzzes: OPEN 'TIL SOMEONE LEAVES.

JOSEFINA, 28, in a rain-soaked red coat, sits alone at the counter slurping noodles. CASPIAN, 30, in a bicycle courier's jacket, drips onto the stool next to hers. WREN, 60s, the owner, wipes the counter. BASIL, 20s, the dishwasher, drags a bus tub of bowls through the kitchen door.

CASPIAN
Is this seat free?

JOSEFINA
It's a counter.

CASPIAN
That's not a no.

JOSEFINA
That's a counter.

He sits. Wren sets a bowl in front of him without being asked.

WREN
Caspian. Usual.

CASPIAN
Thanks, Wren.

JOSEFINA
You're a regular.

CASPIAN
Eleven months.

JOSEFINA
I've been coming for three years.

CASPIAN
I would've remembered.

JOSEFINA
I'm very forgettable.

CASPIAN
You're wearing a red coat.

She looks down at it, then at him. A noodle dangles from her chopsticks. Basil emerges from the kitchen, sees them, and pauses.

BASIL
Wren, do we have more broth?

WREN
Back left.

BASIL
Okay.

He leaves. Josefina and Caspian eat in silence. The neon buzzes.

CASPIAN
I have a question.

JOSEFINA
Okay.

CASPIAN
Why do you sit at the counter?

JOSEFINA
Why do you?

CASPIAN
Because the booths have a wall. You can't see anyone.

JOSEFINA
That's the point.

CASPIAN
Of the booth?

JOSEFINA
Of not wanting to be seen.

A pause. Caspian lays down his chopsticks. He turns his stool slightly toward her.

CASPIAN
Are you hiding?

JOSEFINA
From who?

CASPIAN
I don't know. From the night?

JOSEFINA
That's very poetic.

CASPIAN
It's very late.

JOSEFINA
It's two a.m.

CASPIAN
I know. I've been delivering since six.

JOSEFINA
You work twenty hours?

CASPIAN
Nineteen. I get a nap.

She laughs, a short, startled sound. She covers her mouth, embarrassed, and Wren glances up with a small smile.

JOSEFINA
You're a bad influence.

CASPIAN
You're a good listener.

JOSEFINA
I haven't said anything.

CASPIAN
That's the best kind.

She meets his eyes. A beat. She nudges her half-eaten bowl toward him with one finger.

JOSEFINA
Finish it.

CASPIAN
Are you sure?

JOSEFINA
You've been nineteen hours.

He takes the bowl. Wren sets a second pair of chopsticks beside it. Basil, in the kitchen doorway, shakes his head in awe.

BASIL
(to Wren)
She never shares.

WREN
(to Basil)
Back to the dishes.
